---
import type { APIEntry } from '../lib/reference'
const { entry } = Astro.props as { entry: APIEntry }
const parameters = entry.parameters.map(p => p.name)
const returned = entry.signatures[0]?.match(/\):\s*([^;]+);?$/)?.[1]
const result = returned || (entry.kind === 'class' ? 'Owned native handle' : 'See signature below')
---
<figure class="dataflow">
  <div class="dataflow-row"><div><small>ARGUMENTS</small><strong>{parameters.slice(0, 4).join(', ') || (entry.kind === 'class' ? 'Constructor or factory' : 'See signature below')}</strong></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="operation"><small>{entry.kind.toUpperCase()}</small><strong>{entry.display}</strong></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><small>RETURN TYPE</small><strong>{result}</strong></div></div>
  <figcaption>Call structure. A void return can still write to destination arguments. The parameter descriptions define inputs, outputs and ownership.</figcaption>
</figure>
